WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.150
High above us, in the
stratosphere, lies the ozone layer.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.910
In 1987, the Montreal Protocol began
phasing out the chemicals that destroy it.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:16.350
Over Antarctica, the layer should
recover to 1980 values by about 2066.

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.150
Meanwhile, the climate is warming.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.390
So why might a thinner ozone
layer show up in eye clinics,

6
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.590
and a warmer climate in malaria wards?

7
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.870
Is it city air pollution?

8
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.130
Or are these diseases nothing to
do with the environment at all?

9
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.990
In this mission, you'll trace a chain
from thinning ozone to the human body.

10
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.790
Then you'll follow a warming climate
into the body's heat balance,

11
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.350
into disease, and into food.

12
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.170
Your mission: explain how a changing
global environment reaches eye clinics and

13
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.350
malaria wards.
